.TH LIBRDP-SERVER 7 "2026-07-16" "librdp 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
librdp-server \- embeddable RDP listener and peer state machine
.SH DESCRIPTION
The librdp server API is declared in
.BR <librdp/server.h> .
It allows applications to create a listening socket, accept peers, and drive
the server-side negotiation and activation state machine with
.BR librdp_server_peer_run_once ().
.P
The application owns security policy, desktop model, graphics production,
and resource access. The library owns the listener, peer transport, MCS/GCC
state, activation sequencing, runtime input delivery, static-channel dispatch,
and BGRA surface update serialization for each peer handle.
.SH OBJECTS
.TP
.B librdp_server_config
Versioned listener configuration. Strings are copied when the server object is
created.
.TP
.B librdp_server
Opaque listener handle.
.TP
.B librdp_server_peer
Opaque accepted-peer handle.
.SH LIFECYCLE
A typical server application initializes
.BR librdp_server_config ,
creates a server with
.BR librdp_server_new (),
starts listening with
.BR librdp_server_listen (),
accepts peers with
.BR librdp_server_accept (),
drives each peer with
.BR librdp_server_peer_run_once (),
updates the peer surface with
.BR librdp_server_peer_desktop_width (),
.BR librdp_server_peer_desktop_height (),
.BR librdp_server_peer_surface_blit_bgra32 ()
and
.BR librdp_server_peer_surface_present (),
and frees each handle with
.BR librdp_server_peer_free ()
and
.BR librdp_server_free ().
.SH STATES
Peer states include listening setup, X.224 negotiation, MCS connection,
domain ready, user attached, channel joining, activation, active, closing, and
closed. Use
.BR librdp_server_peer_get_state ()
to observe the current state.
.SH THREADING
Server and peer handles are not internally synchronized. Applications should
drive each peer from one owner thread or provide external locking.
.SH SECURITY
Do not expose a listener on an untrusted network without an explicit
authentication and TLS policy. Trace output is redacted by default and must not
be used for credentials or raw user payloads.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
build/librdp-example-server-listener --bind 127.0.0.1 --port 3390 --width 1024 --height 768
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-tracing (7)
